          alt: "The drug chart is the commonest reversible cause — in an older person the same dose is a bigger dose because kidney clearance falls even when the creatinine looks normal, less muscle and more fat change where drugs go, and the brain is more sensitive to sedation, so start low, go slow and review; the prescribing cascade in which a side effect is treated as a new disease; and the groups of drugs that repay a second look.",
